01:35:39,150 --> 01:35:49,668
In this module, we'll explore what Langchain is, why it's become essential for building Gen AI applications, and how it fits into the broader AI ecosystem.

688
01:35:50,126 --> 01:35:54,532
Let's start by understanding what Langchain actually is and why it exists.

689
01:35:55,438 --> 01:36:04,388
Langchain is a framework and ecosystem for building applications with large language models, providing structured building blocks and integrations.

690
01:36:05,134 --> 01:36:11,012
It's not a full production system, but offers reusable components for LLM-based apps.

691
01:36:11,790 --> 01:36:14,788
Using an LLM as a chatbot is limiting.

692
01:36:15,310 --> 01:36:19,744
Real applications need data, tools, context, and control.

693
01:36:20,526 --> 01:36:34,064
Langchain integrates LLM into broader workflows, addressing challenges like databases, APIs, and external tools, while leaving credentials, permissions, and failure handling to the developer.

694
01:36:34,350 --> 01:36:42,308
Langchain transforms language models into system components, offering scaffolding for applications beyond text generation.

695
01:36:43,150 --> 01:36:53,956
It excels in integration, connecting models to databases, APIs, documents, and tools, seamlessly integrating AI with your existing infrastructure.

696
01:36:54,350 --> 01:37:05,732
With multimodal support, Langchain works with various providers like GPT, Claude, Llama, and more, allowing flexibility to switch models without rewriting code.

697
01:37:06,126 --> 01:37:20,100
It also provides workflow management, orchestrating complex operations such as chaining calls, managing dynamic prompts, context, and tool coordination, making AI applications more scalable and efficient.

698
01:37:20,590 --> 01:37:22,148
So we know what Langchain is.

699
01:37:22,862 --> 01:37:28,356
Now let's talk about why it's become the go to framework for building serious LLM applications.

700
01:37:29,166 --> 01:37:30,660
What makes it so valuable?

701
01:37:31,470 --> 01:37:35,780
First, Langchain excels at chaining multiple language models together.

702
01:37:36,398 --> 01:37:42,564
This means you can connect different models in a sequence to create sophisticated multi-step workflows.

703
01:37:42,958 --> 01:37:58,436
Instead of forcing one model to do everything, you can use GPT-4 for complex reasoning, a smaller model for simple classifications, and a specialized model for embeddings, all in the same application, orchestrated seamlessly.

704
01:37:59,022 --> 01:38:01,280
Second, external tool integration.

705
01:38:01,486 --> 01:38:02,372
This is huge.

706
01:38:02,862 --> 01:38:08,452
Langchain provides seamless connections to databases, APIs, and web scraping services.

707
01:38:08,974 --> 01:38:11,972
Your LLM is no longer stuck just generating text.

708
01:38:12,526 --> 01:38:20,356
It can pull real data from ASQL database, call a weather API, scrape a website, whatever your application needs.

709
01:38:20,782 --> 01:38:24,260
Third, multimodal support with a unified interface.

710
01:38:24,910 --> 01:38:31,760
Whether you're using GPT, Claude, or an open source model, Langchain provides consistent abstractions.

711
01:38:32,000 --> 01:38:39,716
This makes it incredibly easy to switch between models or use multiple models in the same application without rewriting your code.

712
01:38:40,206 --> 01:38:42,468
Your application logic stays the same.

713
01:38:43,566 --> 01:38:46,244
Fourth, dynamic prompt management.

714
01:38:47,054 --> 01:38:55,364
Instead of hard coding prompts as strings, Langchain has built-in support for complex prompt generation and template management.

715
01:38:56,174 --> 01:39:02,628
This is crucial when you need prompts that adapt based on context, user input, or retrieve data.

716
01:39:03,054 --> 01:39:07,332
The framework handles the complexity of building these dynamic prompts for you.

717
01:39:08,046 --> 01:39:11,460
Fifth, real-time external data integration.

718
01:39:12,142 --> 01:39:18,692
