3382
06:16:10,958 --> 06:16:16,196
Now, the agent immediately explains that it cannot log in or use credentials on my behalf.

3383
06:16:16,590 --> 06:16:18,048
And this is not a failure.

3384
06:16:18,286 --> 06:16:21,092
It is intentional safety and privacy boundaries.

3385
06:16:21,550 --> 06:16:25,764
However, instead of stopping completely, the agent does something intelligent.

3386
06:16:26,222 --> 06:16:33,572
That is, it switches to publicly available information and clearly tells us what it can and cannot access.

3387
06:16:34,158 --> 06:16:44,608
So it explains LinkedIn learning subscription model, lists publicly visible AI courses, and provides approximate pricing, all without crossing security boundaries.

3388
06:16:44,942 --> 06:16:54,084
So the key takeaway here is Auto GPT Agent works well with public data, but anything behind a login requires human involvement.

3389
06:16:54,958 --> 06:16:59,328
Now I'll show you what happens when the goal itself is very unclear.

3390
06:16:59,630 --> 06:17:02,208
So agents don't guess intent well.

3391
06:17:02,510 --> 06:17:05,008
Ambiguity leads to unpredictable results.

3392
06:17:05,230 --> 06:17:07,648
I have told this many times throughout this session.

3393
06:17:08,078 --> 06:17:11,648
So you can see this prompt intentionally lacks specificity.

3394
06:17:11,886 --> 06:17:15,748
There's no clear scope, no constraints, and no defined output.

3395
06:17:16,270 --> 06:17:23,492
I'll execute this prompt now and watch how the agent struggles to decide what exactly to research or how deep to go.

3396
06:17:24,238 --> 06:17:25,728
Now let's look at the output.

3397
06:17:26,062 --> 06:17:28,368
The goal I gave the agent was very broad.

3398
06:17:28,622 --> 06:17:34,372
Research AI tools and give the insights, without specifying the scope, depth, or audience.

3399
06:17:35,086 --> 06:17:37,728
Because of that, notice what the agent does.

3400
06:17:38,062 --> 06:17:46,048
It asks clarifying questions first, and when allowed to proceed, it produces a very wide, generic market overview.

3401
06:17:46,446 --> 06:17:50,436
The output is not wrong, but it's not sharply focused either.

3402
06:17:50,766 --> 06:17:56,128
As you can see, we get categories, pricing ranges, trends, and examples.

3403
06:17:56,462 --> 06:18:00,996
But no clear prioritization or decision-ready insights is there.

3404
06:18:01,582 --> 06:18:04,420
So this demonstrates an important principle.

3405
06:18:04,782 --> 06:18:07,780
Agents don't infer intent the way humans do.

3406
06:18:08,048 --> 06:18:13,156
If the goal is not precise, the output becomes broad and sometimes overwhelming.

3407
06:18:13,568 --> 06:18:18,724
So when working with agents, clarity up front directly controls output quality.

3408
06:18:19,088 --> 06:18:21,728
Agents rely heavily on page structure.

3409
06:18:21,968 --> 06:18:26,820
If the website layout is complex or inconsistent, extraction can go wrong.

3410
06:18:27,248 --> 06:18:30,564
So this is the next limitation, which I'm going to demonstrate to you.

3411
06:18:31,008 --> 06:18:38,724
As you can see, this prompt asks the agent to extract structured data from pages with varying layout, which often causes mismatches.

3412
06:18:39,246 --> 06:18:40,068
I'll run this now.

3413
06:18:40,608 --> 06:18:45,540
Notice that some prices may be missing, incorrect, or mismatched with products.

3414
06:18:46,048 --> 06:18:49,888
This output is a great example of partial success with caveats.

3415
06:18:50,288 --> 06:18:56,196
The agent attempted to extract prices across multiple e commerce platforms, which is a complex task.

3416
06:18:56,528 --> 06:19:05,444
Notice how it openly states that real time scraping is not possible and instead relies on publicly available listings, aggregators, and reported prices.

3417
06:19:06,158 --> 06:19:13,712
Also observe the wide price range, especially for flagship products like iPhones and MacBooks, which I gave as an input here.

3418
06:19:14,094 --> 06:19:21,872
This happens because e-commerce sites have dynamic pricing, regional variations, third-party sellers, and frequent discounts.

3419
06:19:22,254 --> 06:19:27,552
The agent does its best to normalize this, but the output clearly shows inconsistencies.

3420
06:19:27,982 --> 06:19:30,020
This teaches us an important lesson.

3421
06:19:30,382 --> 06:19:38,672
Agents are excellent for approximate comparisons and trend level insights, but not for legally binding or real-time pricing decisions.

3422
06:19:39,022 --> 06:19:42,436
Human verification is still required for final confirmation.

3423
06:19:42,990 --> 06:19:45,552
Agents perform per the instructions they receive.

3424
06:19:45,806 --> 06:19:48,992
So when instructions are shallow, outputs are also shallow.

3425
06:19:49,294 --> 06:19:50,756
So you can see the prompt here.

3426
06:19:51,118 --> 06:19:56,672
This prompt asks for a report, but does not define the structure, depth, or expectations.

3427
06:19:57,102 --> 06:19:58,660
Now I'll execute this prompt.

3428
06:19:59,022 --> 06:20:06,404
You'll see the output is high level and incomplete, not because the agent lacks ability, but because the instruction itself lacks clarity.

3429
06:20:07,054 --> 06:20:12,612
Now, this output might look impressive, and it is, but let's analyze it carefully.

3430
06:20:12,992 --> 06:20:24,900
The agent generated a very long, comprehensive report covering definitions, types, examples, frameworks, use cases, risks, and even further outlook.

3431
06:20:25,312 --> 06:20:28,996
However, notice that no structure constraints were given.

3432
06:20:29,552 --> 06:20:35,108
No target audience, no length limit, no emphasis areas were told in the prompt.

3433
06:20:35,598 --> 06:20:41,700
As a result, the agent produced an academic-style report, which may be too heavy for some audience.

3434
06:20:42,062 --> 06:20:43,232
This is not an error.

3435
06:20:43,438 --> 06:20:46,660
It's a natural result of a broad goal without boundaries.

3436
06:20:47,086 --> 06:20:49,072
So the lesson here is simple.

3437
06:20:49,454 --> 06:20:55,332
When prompts lack structure, agents defer to maximum coverage, not maximum relevance.

3438
06:20:55,790 --> 06:21:00,772
If you want concise, decision-ready output, you must explicitly ask for it.

3439
06:21:01,678 --> 06:21:06,512
Agent mode is powerful, but it operates with strict safety and technical boundaries.

3440
06:21:06,958 --> 06:21:09,636
Let's walk through some common limitations you'll encounter.

3441
06:21:10,222 --> 06:21:16,032
First, agent mode cannot bypass CAPTCHAS, login forms, or two-step authentication.

3442
06:21:16,430 --> 06:21:21,540
If you instruct it to open a dashboard requiring credentials, it will stop and ask for clarification.

3443
06:21:22,350 --> 06:21:25,636
Second, it may occasionally misclick UI elements.

3444
06:21:26,254 --> 06:21:31,908
For example, a button or section may appear similar to another element, leading to incorrect navigation.

3445
06:21:32,526 --> 06:21:39,460
This is because the agent interprets web pages visually, but may not fully understand the dynamic layout of it.

3446
06:21:40,014 --> 06:21:44,912
Agent mode also struggles with JavaScript-heavy or highly interactive websites.

3447
06:21:45,326 --> 06:21:53,380
Pages that load content dynamically or require drag and drop or complex menus can cause the agent to miss key elements.

3448
06:21:53,966 --> 06:21:58,032
It also cannot perform background monitoring or schedule tasks.

3449
06:21:58,382 --> 06:22:05,072
For example, if you ask it to track stock prices every morning, it's not possible without external automation tools.

3450
06:22:05,486 --> 06:22:08,548
Agent mode only acts during the current task window.

3451
06:22:09,198 --> 06:22:14,512
Lastly, the agent operates in a sandbox, meaning file system access is restricted.

3452
06:22:14,766 --> 06:22:20,228
It cannot download files to your computer unless explicitly supported by ChatGPT tools.

3453
06:22:20,654 --> 06:22:27,268
These limitations exist to maintain safety, fairness, and technical consistency across websites and user environments.

3454
06:22:27,726 --> 06:22:30,912
Now let me demonstrate all these limitations in reality for you.

3455
06:22:31,342 --> 06:22:36,100
Agent Mode can browse, but it cannot bypass captchas or even verification steps.

3456
06:22:36,942 --> 06:22:39,232
This is a hard safety limitation.

3457
06:22:39,566 --> 06:22:43,236
This prompt will lead the agent to a site protected by CAPTCHAS.

3458
06:22:43,790 --> 06:22:50,191
The site URL, which I have given here, is cloudflare.com forward slash products hyphen products.

3459
06:22:51,374 --> 06:22:52,512
Now I'll run this.

3460
06:22:53,294 --> 06:22:57,732
Notice that one CAPTCHA appears, the agent cannot proceed further.

3461
06:22:58,190 --> 06:23:03,172
As expected, the agent was able to reach the website but stopped once the CAPTCHA appeared.

3462
06:23:03,758 --> 06:23:07,680
So I tried to fetch the information without logging into the website.

3463
06:23:07,982 --> 06:23:09,988
So this shows a hard limitation.

3464
06:23:10,446 --> 06:23:14,480
Agent mode cannot solve or bypass human verification steps.

3465
06:23:14,830 --> 06:23:18,756
Any workflow that depends on CAPTCHA completion will fail at this point.

3466
06:23:19,534 --> 06:23:24,640
Next limitation is that agent mode interprets UI visually, not semantically.

3467
06:23:25,038 --> 06:23:27,760
If a button looks similar, mistakes can happen.

3468
06:23:28,110 --> 06:23:32,560
It may not be necessary every time it happens, but it may happen in some cases.

3469
06:23:32,910 --> 06:23:40,000
So as you can see the prompt here, this prompt does not guide the agent clearly on which UI elements to prioritize.

3470
06:23:40,334 --> 06:23:43,780
It just says navigate a website and extract pricing information.

3471
06:23:44,366 --> 06:23:45,680
I'll run this prompt now.

3472
06:23:45,998 --> 06:23:49,600
Watch how the agent may click unintended buttons or links.

3473
06:23:49,998 --> 06:23:58,500
Here, the agent attempted to navigate the page and click the correct element, though sometimes it might click unintended elements and go to the wrong solution.

3474
06:23:58,958 --> 06:24:10,080
Since agent mode relies on visual patterns rather than semantic understanding, similar-looking buttons can confuse sometimes, although it was not the case right now when I tried executing.

3475
06:24:10,414 --> 06:24:15,716
So this highlights why precise UI guidance is critical in browser-based prompts.

3476
06:24:16,334 --> 06:24:20,720
Some modern websites rely heavily on JavaScript for rendering content.

3477
06:24:21,102 --> 06:24:25,040
Agent mode may fail to load or extract such pages correctly.

3478
06:24:25,486 --> 06:24:31,556
As you can see in this prompt, this prompt sends the agent to a JavaScript heavy page without fallback instructions.

3479
06:24:32,046 --> 06:24:37,668
So the website it is asking it to navigate is to app.airtable.com or Figma.com.

3480
06:24:38,094 --> 06:24:39,600
Now I will run this prompt.

3481
06:24:39,918 --> 06:24:43,120
You may notice missing or partially loaded content.

3482
06:24:43,470 --> 06:24:47,440
The agent struggled to fully load or extract content from this page.

3483
06:24:47,790 --> 06:24:55,280
As you can see in the output, highly JavaScript-driven interfaces often render dynamically, which agent mode may not handle reliably.

3484
06:24:55,630 --> 06:25:00,068
So as a result, the extracted data can be incomplete or missing entirely.

3485
06:25:00,718 --> 06:25:06,724
So it is missing entirely in this case, as it is mentioned that the site unavailable message was there.

3486
06:25:07,200 --> 06:25:12,260
Talking about the next limitation, agent mode does not have unlimited memory.

3487
06:25:12,654 --> 06:25:16,480
Long workflows can cause earlier context to be forgotten as well.

3488
06:25:16,878 --> 06:25:23,760
So as you can see the prompt here, which I am using, this prompt intentionally spans too many steps without checkpoints.

3489
06:25:24,078 --> 06:25:31,440
As I am mentioning here, perform a long multi-step research task across many websites and summarize everything at the end.

3490
06:25:31,822 --> 06:25:33,988
There's no proper steps to find over here.

3491
06:25:34,766 --> 06:25:36,356
Now I will execute this.

3492
06:25:37,358 --> 06:25:43,280
So you will notice how earlier details may be lost or summarized poorly in some cases.

3493
06:25:43,694 --> 06:25:50,000
So during this long multi-step task, earlier details are either forgotten or overly summarized.

3494
06:25:50,318 --> 06:25:52,644
As you can see, it is overly summarized.

3495
06:25:53,390 --> 06:25:57,440
Agent mode has limited working memory across extended workflows.

3496
06:25:57,678 --> 06:26:02,308
This makes it unsuitable for long research chains without intermediate checkpoints.

3497
06:26:03,040 --> 06:26:05,440
Agent Mode works in session only.

3498
06:26:05,710 --> 06:26:08,720
It cannot run tasks continuously in the background.

3499
06:26:09,070 --> 06:26:12,320
This is another limitation, which I am going to demonstrate it to you.

3500
06:26:12,686 --> 06:26:19,680
So as you can see the prompt here, this prompt requests ongoing execution, which agent mode cannot support.

3501
06:26:20,142 --> 06:26:22,436
Let us actually see what happens in the output.

3502
06:26:22,926 --> 06:26:25,040
So I will execute this prompt now.

3503
06:26:25,454 --> 06:26:31,280
So according to me, the agent should explain that it cannot perform persistent or scheduled background tasks.

3504
06:26:31,630 --> 06:26:33,572
Let us see what output we get at the end.

3505
06:26:34,080 --> 06:26:39,364
The agent clearly states that it cannot monitor websites continuously or run on a schedule.

3506
06:26:39,982 --> 06:26:43,200
Agent mode operates only within the active session.

3507
06:26:43,502 --> 06:26:48,996
Any requirement for background execution or periodic monitoring is outside its capability.

3508
06:26:49,678 --> 06:26:52,900
As you can see, it is also clearly mentioned in the output.

3509
06:26:53,454 --> 06:26:57,700
To ensure your agents perform reliably, follow these best practices.

3510
06:26:58,190 --> 06:27:03,920
The first and most important role is to create clear, structured prompts, which are very important.

3511
06:27:04,462 --> 06:27:07,588
Agents perform best when they know exactly what you want.

3512
06:27:08,206 --> 06:27:11,520
Next is to break the complex task into smaller parts.

3513
06:27:11,854 --> 06:27:20,548
Instead of asking for a complete report in one go, start with like gather sources, or maybe extract key points, and then generate the summary.

3514
06:27:21,294 --> 06:27:25,200
Providing examples of expected output dramatically improves quality.

3515
06:27:25,486 --> 06:27:31,556
Whether it is a sample table, a writing style, or a slide format, the agent uses this as a blueprint.

3516
06:27:32,174 --> 06:27:35,840
Adding checkpoints ensures the agent pauses at logical intervals.

3517
06:27:36,080 --> 06:27:39,940
This prevents major errors and gives you control over workflow directions.

3518
06:27:40,430 --> 06:27:46,116
Finally, always ask the agent to state its assumptions before beginning execution.

3519
06:27:46,574 --> 06:27:50,660
This one step catches misunderstandings early and saves time.

3520
06:27:51,566 --> 06:27:58,512
These practices collectively reduce errors, improve consistency, and create smooth agentic workflow.

3521
06:27:58,672 --> 06:28:01,604
And that's a wrap on this Agentic AI course.

